rota lap 5009, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the concrete fact at the door was df: 83G free, 51 percent, 5,528 entries in /tmp, and it named the lap
think reds first: %745 stands OPEN and its own last line names the remainder -- counting the other leakers is its own lap, and that half is ungated
think shared_pen asks whether a pen is contended; pen_entry asks whether it is entered; nothing asks whether it is released, and one pen is one object with three failure modes
think the sharper finding is population rather than predicate: pen_entry reads .sh names and POSIX shebangs, and the Rishi witness that filled the pier carries neither, so the leaker was outside the family rather than passing inside it
think claimed before building, since the port_registry and port_band pair cost two ships a build each on 20260911
obs never_removed is a ratchet at 16 rather than a wall -- fourteen of the sixteen are amphora and caravan witnesses whose repair belongs to their own lanes, and a wall here would red every ship for faults no lap of theirs may touch
obs unreleased_on_refusal at 336 is reported and gated by nothing: in shell the cure is one EXIT trap, and Rishi has no trap at all, so that half is a language question rather than one line
obs the scan's list and the pier's litter agree -- the six amphora leakers account for 133 of 629 standing pens, which is the cross-check a count of tracked bytes alone could never give
obs three faults first residency found in the reading itself, each planted as a leg before the number was trusted: the one-line sh -c pen lifetime, the rmdir release, and a prefilter that made the standing half structurally unable to see its second spelling
obs two reds stand on every ship's cold pass and neither is mine -- rune_assert_sweep one over its ceiling, and bearing_quorum's three files misfiled into room m; named rather than moved
